1. Introduction
In this experiment, I learned the basics of Large Language Models (LLMs) and how to interact with them through a Python application.
The main aim was to understand how an application communicates with an LLM and receives responses based on user input.

2. What I Did
Created a Python project for making an LLM call.
Understood the basic structure of an LLM-powered application.
Learned how to provide input to a language model.
Explored how the model processes the input and generates a response.
Worked with Python files and project dependencies.
Executed the program and observed the generated output.

3. What I Understood
Through this experiment, I understood:
Large Language Models: LLMs are AI models that understand and generate human-like text.
Prompt: A prompt is the input or instruction given to the model.
LLM API: An API allows our Python application to communicate with a language model.
Model Response: The model processes the prompt and sends a generated response back to the application.
Python Integration: Python can be used to connect applications with LLM services.

4. What I Learned
How LLMs can be integrated into Python applications.
How user input is sent to a language model.
How to receive and display generated responses.
The basic workflow of an LLM application.
How to organize a Python project and manage dependencies.

5. Challenges Faced
During this experiment, I explored the setup required for running an LLM application, understood the project structure, and learned how to resolve basic execution and configuration issues.

6. Learning Outcome
By completing this experiment, I gained a basic understanding of LLM integration and how Python applications can communicate with language models to generate responses.
This experiment helped me build a foundation for developing more advanced Generative AI applications in the upcoming practical sessions.


   
